Third-party content redistributed in this repository:

The rendered benchmark reports under `docs/reports/` are self-contained HTML
pages with their JavaScript inlined rather than fetched, so that a page opens
with no network and still renders years later. Each therefore embeds a copy of
Plotly.js and its dependencies, which carry their own licences (MIT, and others
named in the bundle's own notices). Those files are redistributed unmodified and
are not covered by the copyright above; their licence headers travel inside each
page. Plotly.js is Copyright (c) Plotly, Inc., MIT licensed.

The engine itself vendors nothing: `zig build` links no third-party code. The
analysis tooling's Python dependencies are declared in `bench/pyproject.toml`
and pinned by `bench/uv.lock`, and are fetched rather than redistributed here.

The load generator `qdrant/bfb` is fetched and built, not redistributed here.
The one patch this project carried against it — findings 32's `--rps` reaping
fix — was authored here and merged upstream as qdrant/bfb#172, so `BFB_PIN`
names a plain upstream commit and no fork is vendored.
